SeedSignerOS: skip the portmidi fallback when the midi feature is disabled

On a cross build (buildroot) with -Dmidi=disabled, meson still enters the
portmidi fallback branch: cc.find_library('portmidi', required: <false>)
returns a not-found library, but the surrounding declare_dependency() is
reported as found(), so `if portmidi_dep.found()` in src_c/meson.build is
true and the pypm extension is built anyway. That fallback is also the only
dependency whose include_directories come from pg_inc_dirs (every other dep
resolves via pkg-config), and pg_inc_dirs is seeded from bases that include
/usr/local -- so pypm is compiled with -I/usr/local/include, which buildroot's
cross gcc rejects with "unsafe header/library path used in cross-compilation",
failing the build.

Gate the fallback on get_option('midi').enabled(): with midi disabled the
dependency stays the (not-found) pkg-config result, pypm is skipped, and no
/usr path leaks into the compile. Behaviour is unchanged whenever midi is
enabled/auto and portmidi is genuinely present.

Upstream-issue: https://github.com/pygame-community/pygame-ce/issues (cross
build with midi disabled still compiles pypm via the /usr/local fallback).

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -450,7 +450,7 @@
 endif # emscripten
 
 portmidi_dep = dependency('portmidi', required: false)
-if not portmidi_dep.found() and not plat.startswith('emscripten')
+if get_option('midi').enabled() and not portmidi_dep.found() and not plat.startswith('emscripten')
     portmidi_dep = declare_dependency(
         include_directories: pg_inc_dirs,
         dependencies: cc.find_library(
